<p>Britain said it tracked three Russian submarines during a month-long operation in the North Atlantic near undersea cables and pipelines. Defence Secretary John Healey described the activity as a suspected intelligence-gathering mission focused on critical infrastructure. Healey said the UK worked with Norway and other allies, using warships, patrol aircraft, and helicopters, and stressed that officials found no evidence of damage to subsea infrastructure. British officials said the submarines included one Akula-class nuclear-powered attack submarine and two specialist vessels from Russia’s Main Directorate of Deep Sea Research, or GUGI, which the UK says is designed to survey underwater infrastructure in peacetime. London said it made the operation public to deter further activity and signal that any attempt to damage cables or pipelines would bring serious consequences, amid broader tensions with Russia over European security and infrastructure protection.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/xSfAWSx6vO7LXHtyZhpDbPdq13DOeAwiMfaXJza1z2yZdt5FWMBGFlL_ckbSztyvNCG5LaZjltjECpLzi8ask_aLqq0Tm7hey4F17ZaCOBWA' alt='This undated handout image release on April 9, 2026 by Britain’s Royal Navy shows Russia’s kilo-class submarine Krasnodar at sea.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Allied mission: The UK said it carried out the surveillance effort with Norway and other unnamed allies, underscoring cross-border coordination to monitor North Atlantic infrastructure routes.</li><li>No damage found: UK officials said they found no evidence that the Russian operation damaged cables or pipelines.</li></ul><blockquote>We see your activity over our cables and our pipelines and you should know that any attempt to damage them will not be tolerated and will have serious consequences. - John Healey</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UK Defence Ministry: British officials said they tracked and deterred the submarines to expose what they saw as malign activity and to show that UK forces had monitored the vessels throughout the operation. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cre13qn9z7do'>BBC</a>)</li><li>John Healey: Healey said the UK disclosed the operation as a deterrent, making clear that any threat to subsea infrastructure had been detected and would draw a response. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/09/world/europe/uk-russia-submarines-cables.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Defence analysts cited by Dawn: The reports describe GUGI as one of Russia’s most secretive organizations, responsible for deep-ocean monitoring and mini-sub capabilities that make undersea infrastructure a strategic focus. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1990364/britain-accuses-russia-of-covert-op-in-north-atlantic'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/09/world/europe/uk-russia-submarines-cables.html'>3 Russian Submarines Detected Near Britain Were Spying, U.K. Says</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3349565/uk-tracked-russia-submarines-alleged-atlantic-covert-operation-defence-secretary'>UK tracked Russia submarines in alleged Atlantic ‘covert’ operation: defence secretary</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/britain-russia-submarines-healey-undersea-infrastructure-tension/33728781.html'>London Says It Tracked Three Russian Submarines Near Critical Undersea Infrastructure</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1990364/britain-accuses-russia-of-covert-op-in-north-atlantic'>Britain accuses Russia of ‘covert’ op in North Atlantic</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cre13qn9z7do'>UK says Russia ran submarine operation over cables and pipelines</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/04/09/uk-defense-ministry-says-3-russian-submarines-conducted-suspicious-activity-near-undersea-cables-in-north-atlantic'>UK Defense Ministry says 3 Russian submarines conducted suspicious activity near undersea cables in North Atlantic</a> - meduza.io</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cg54mdlqppjt'>British defence secretary John Healey says three Russian Navy submarines engaged in covert operations against the UK in the North Sea near its undersea cables and says counter-measures are underway.</a> - bbc.co.uk</li></ul>